        "date": "2026-11-07T22:21:58Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): Tormach PathPilot post and 770MX machine; machine units reach posts\n\nA Tormach PathPilot (LinuxCNC-dialect) 3-axis post and a Tormach 770MX\nmachine file in inches, from Tormach's and LinuxCNC's public docs.\nThe post writes no % fence and no O word, states G91.1 and a G64 P\ntolerance, a G30 before every tool change, G43 H from the tool table,\ndwell P in seconds, G84 tapping, a belt-range comment for speeds only\none 770 belt range serves, refuses tool numbers outside 1-1000, and\nends Z-up, G30, M30 as PathPilot's own programs do.\n\nMachine files could already state inches, but the parser dropped the\nunit after scaling to mm. Machine gains `units` (Some(\"inch\") when the\nfile states inches; skipped when None, so project files are unchanged),\nand the post mirror and script_props expose it as `machine.units`; the\nTormach post writes G20 and inch values from it. Other posts ignore it.\n\nRefs #131\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
