      },
      "message": "fix(post): position X Y with Z up before the first Tormach move\n\nX and Y are unknown at program start and after every G30, so the first\nmove after a tool change started wherever the table happened to be; the\nPathPilot Hub simulator (v2.14.4) flags it: \"Axis XY not specified by\nthis or previous motions, end point will depend on current position\".\nThat move is now preceded by a G0 to its X Y alone at the current, Z-up\nheight (a rapid's target, a feed or arc's stream start point, a cycle's\nfirst hole), PathPilot's own XY-first order, and only then does Z come\ndown. Each Tormach golden gains that one line.\n\nRefs #131\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
