        "date": "2026-11-08T00:49:47Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): rapid to the start height before the first Tormach feed\n\nFound on the 770MX: a Face's first move is a plunge FEED from its\nclearance start. After the tool change (G53 G0 Z0, G30) Z stands at the\ntop of travel, so the posted program fed the whole stroke at the plunge\nrate (11.81 in/min). Once X Y are positioned, the post now rapids Z down\nto the stream's start height - where the generator says the tool already\nstands - and the feed runs only the stretch it planned. A program with\nthis line added by hand ran correctly on the machine.\n\nPinned by tormach_post::a_face_job_on_the_built_in_770mx_passes_the_gate_and_posts_inch\n(fails without the fix). face_square_40x40's golden gains the rapid.\n\nRefs #131\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
